---
title: Run mapping · another home's run
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    classDef ok stroke-width:1.6px
    classDef wait stroke-width:1.6px
    classDef fail stroke-width:1.6px

    [*] --> foreign
    foreign --> check : home at recorded path?
    state check <<choice>>
    check --> records : [same identity]
    check --> gone : [absent, file, other dir]
    records --> released : [clean stop recorded]
    records --> refused : [live, unproven]
    gone --> scan : release --expect-selection
    state scan <<choice>>
    scan --> released : [no process of it]
    scan --> refused : [process names path]
    released --> [*]

    note right of gone
        Records went with the home.
        Owner gone, selection digest
        names the path's state.
    end note
    note right of released
        Mapping, restart intent and
        down hooks kept in an audit
        file, then removed.
    end note
    note left of refused
        Names each PID or what is
        unproven. A moved home run
        from its new path is not
        seen: release again there.
    end note

    class released ok
    class gone wait
    class refused fail
